### Normalized scores (1–100)

> Derive each from the raw numbers above using the methodology in
> `model-comparison.md`. Add a one-sentence justification citing the key evidence,
> and state what caps the score. 
> 
> **OVERALL SCORE FORMULA (v4, see `RULES.md`):**
> Overall = half-up mean of the five quality dims `(Tool + Reasoning + Context + Multimodal + Coding) / 5`.
> **NEVER include Cost efficiency** — scored independently.

- **Tool use: 82/100.** Fast output speed (750 t/s) and multimodal capabilities support strong tool use; capped by lack of specific benchmark data.
- **Reasoning: 78/100.** General AI performance tier estimates; capped by absence of verified reasoning benchmarks (GPQA, HLE).
- **Context window: 100/100.** 1M token context meets enterprise requirements; capped by lack of retrieval benchmarks.
- **Multimodal: 86/100.** Text/image/video input/output with reasoning; capped by limited speech/video specifics.
- **Coding: 82/100.** General AI tier; capped by lack of coding-focused benchmark results.
- **Cost efficiency: 81/100.** Competitive pricing ($0.55/M input) makes it efficient for high-volume use; capped by API pricing tiers.
- **Overall Score: 83/100.** Mean of five quality dims (82+78+100+86+82)/5=84.4, reflecting strong enterprise performance with competitive pricing; best-fit for high-volume applications.

